<part xml:id="operations-research-optimisation">
  <title>Operations Research &amp; Optimisation</title>

  <chapter xml:id="operations-research-one">
    <title>Operations Research I</title>

    <section xml:id="or-introduction">
      <title>Introduction to Operations Research</title>
      <p>Operations research uses mathematical models to support decisions involving limited resources, competing objectives and constraints.</p>
    </section>

    <section xml:id="or-modelling">
      <title>Mathematical Modelling</title>
      <p>This section develops decision variables, objective functions, constraints and model interpretation.</p>
    </section>

    <section xml:id="or-linear-programming">
      <title>Linear Programming</title>
      <p>Lecture material covering the same mathematical idea will be consolidated here rather than preserved as separate lecture pages.</p>
    </section>
  </chapter>
</part>
